---
import { cardCls, emptyCls } from '../lib/ui';
// The $100 bet (#/bet; thorp/bet.py, /api/bet): Justin's bet (2026-11-07, 20:10) that a ladder of model sizes,
// each rung proved on this Mac, makes a 350m trained for $100 on a rented H100 bet the right way on quantum
// physics. Read-only: the theory, the ladder with each rung's goal, time and cost, the discrete-atom test and
// its chain, where the $100 goes, the gates before it is spent, and the risks. UI.md, "The $100 bet".
---
<div class="section" id="bet">
  <h1>$100 <span class="q">the bet: a ladder of model sizes, each rung proved on this Mac, makes a 350m trained for $100 on a rented H100 bet the right way on quantum physics</span></h1>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
    <h2>The bet <span class="note">Justin's words, and what $100 buys on one rented H100</span></h2>
    <div id="betclaim"><div class={emptyCls()}>reading the bet…</div></div>
  </section>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
    <h2 id="betstorytitle">On the Orient pier <span class="note">the bet as Quentin Luck tells it to the bergies and car guards</span></h2>
    <div class="betstory" id="betstory"></div>
  </section>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
    <h2>The theory <span class="note">why a ladder makes the trader cheap enough to bet on</span></h2>
    <ul class="betlist" id="bettheory"></ul>
  </section>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
    <h2>The ladder <span class="note">each size's goal, what it reads, how long it takes on this Mac and what it would cost rented; the journey from 300k to 50m is what the bet is modelled against</span></h2>
    <div class="scroll"><table id="betladder" data-nosort><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    <p class="note mt" id="betladdernote"></p>
  </section>
  <div class="row">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>The quantum bet <span class="note">the discrete atom, written to the discovery tests' rule</span></h2>
      <div id="betquantum"></div>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>The chain to the discrete atom <span class="note">one rung per size, each resting on the one below</span></h2>
      <div class="scroll"><table id="betchain" data-nosort><thead><tr><th>size</th><th>rung</th><th>what it asks</th></tr></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    </section>
  </div>
  <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
    <h2>Where the $100 goes <span class="note">one H100 sitting: the 350m at twenty tokens a parameter, two seeds and the precursor ablation, as the pass rule asks</span></h2>
    <div class="scroll"><table id="betbudget" data-nosort><thead></thead><tbody></tbody></table></div>
    <p class="note mt" id="betbudgetnote"></p>
  </section>
  <div class="row">
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>Gates before the H100 <span class="note">what must be true before the $100 is spent</span></h2>
      <ul class="betlist" id="betgates"></ul>
    </section>
    <section class={cardCls(false, 'panel')}>
      <h2>What could break it <span class="note">the bet's known risks</span></h2>
      <ul class="betlist" id="betrisks"></ul>
    </section>
  </div>
</div>
